statement:
An increasing subset \(I=\{i_1<\cdots<i_r\}\) corresponds to the partition \((i_r-r,\ldots,i_1-1)\). For dominant integral \(GL_n\) weights \(\lambda,\mu,
u\), the Hermitian eigenvalue inequalities with the trace condition characterize positivity of the Littlewood--Richardson multiplicity \(c_{\lambda\mu}^{
u}\). Equivalence at integral scale uses saturation: \(c_{N\lambda,N\mu}^{N
u}>0\) for some positive integer \(N\) implies \(c_{\lambda\mu}^{
u}>0\).
